{"pageProps":{"page":{"ID":1407,"post_author":"8","post_date":"April 25, 2025","post_date_gmt":"2025-04-25 14:27:43","post_title":"Accessibility Statement","post_status":"publish","comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","post_name":"accessibility","post_modified":"2025-08-25 18:45:38","post_modified_gmt":"2025-08-25 18:45:38","guid":"https://pylonlending.com/?page_id=1407","post_type":"page","filter":"raw","url":"https://pylon-two.vercel.app/accessibility/","header_options":{"header_theme":"grey"},"body_color":"grey","sections":[{"acf_fc_layout":"landing_page","layout":[{"acf_fc_layout":"legal","heading":"Pylon Accessibility Statement","last_updated":"April 25, 2025","content_blocks":[{"acf_fc_layout":"text_block","text":"<h2><b>Accessibility Statement</b></h2>\n<p><b>Our commitment to supporting individuals with disabilities</b></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Embed Inc. d/b/a Pylon, Pylon Lending (“Pylon”), is committed to making our products and services, and those of the businesses we partner with, accessible to meet the needs of all our consumers. We are working to enhance our site and increase accessibility and usability for all consumers.</span></p>\n<p><b>Online and mobile accessibility</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> We strive to follow the globally recognized standards of the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) to provide content that is compatible with computer-based assistive technologies, browsers, and operating systems.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most browsers and/or operating systems have built-in accessibility features that Pylon supports, from the ability to change colors, contrast, and text size to using screen readers and skip controls. Learn tips for customizing your browser and computer setup at the</span><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/WAI/\"> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">W3C Web Accessibility Initiative website</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p><b>Software recommendations and settings</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> We follow W3C&#8217;s globally recognized standards to provide content that’s compatible with the most popular assistive technologies and web browsers. We recommend using the most current version (or the version released just prior to) of the manufacturer&#8217;s assistive technology applications, along with a current version of the operating systems and browsers listed below. We also recommend trying different types of browsers and/or operating systems with assistive technology applications to determine which combination works best for you. You can visit the individual manufacturer’s site for information about how to obtain them. You may also have access to assistance from local and state agencies or non-profit groups in your area.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While we strive to adhere to the W3C’s guidelines and standards for accessibility and usability, we cannot guarantee that any third-party content, feature, software, widgets, plug-ins or tools, located or linked to our website but not owned by Pylon, conform to W3C standards and guidelines, and Pylon shall not be liable for any inaccessibility or usability issues in connection with such.</span></p>\n<p><b>Screen reader applications</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> The following browser and screen reader application pairings are recommended for the best customer experience:</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Chrome and JAWS Mozilla Firefox and NVDA Chrome and TalkBack for Android devices Safari and VoiceOver for iOS and macOS devices</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can improve your online experience by exploring these features and settings available in various assistive technology applications.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Special characters: If it’s required by your screen reading application, enable settings to automatically read any of these special characters: @, #, $, &amp;, &#8216;, &#8220;, /, |, _, { }, [ ] and words with tilde or grave accented characters.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Symbols: If it’s required by your screen reading application, enable settings to automatically read these symbols: +, -, =, *, \\, %, ^, ( ), &lt; and &gt;.</span></p>\n<p><b>Browsers</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> We recommend using the most current version (or the version released just prior to) of Chrome, Firefox, Safari, or Microsoft Edge.</span></p>\n<p><b>Telecommunications relay and teletypewriter services</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Deaf or hard-of-hearing customers can call us using Teletypewriter (TTY/TDD) machines.</span></p>\n<p><b>Accessible statement alternatives</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Upon request, Pylon can arrange for large-print of statements. To request this free service, call (855) 300-8520 to speak to a Pylon representative (or for TTY).</span></p>\n<p><b>Send us accessibility feedback</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> If you’re a person with a disability and would like to send us feedback about accessibility at Pylon, send an email to </span><a href=\"mailto:support@pylonlending.com\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">support@pylonlending.com</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Please don’t include your account or personal information.</span></p>\n<p><b>Contact Information</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Email: </span><a href=\"mailto:support@pylonlending.com\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">support@pylonlending.com</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Telephone: 855-300-8520</span></p>\n"}]}]}],"seo":{"title":"Accessibility Statement - Pylon","description":"Pylon is committed to delivering products and services that are accessible and meet the needs of all of our customers.","image":"https://pylonwp.wpenginepowered.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/pmr.png"},"featured_image":{"src":"https://pylonwp.wpenginepowered.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/pmr.png